==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{der|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*pohjainen}}, equivalent to {{suffix|fi|pohja|inen|t1=bottom, north}}. Adapted from the Savonian dialects, whence the ''-o-'' (compare dialectal {{m|fi|pohjaanen}}), and introduced into the standard language by [[w:fi:Abraham Poppius|Abraham Poppius]]. {{etystub|fi|is the -o- a sound change or the diminutive ending? -oinen?}}

